        "tree_id": "df388b355cc57bbe16d5e69ed3d08fe65d18596d",
        "message": "Product direction: one connector registry, Datadog removed, and the Project record\n\nPRODUCT_DIRECTION.md and ADR-6 to ADR-9 record how the build half and the\ndelivery half become one product (a Project), the connector policy, the\nOperate stage and the order of the next slices.\n\nConnectors are declared once in a registry with the features each one\nfeeds, the pinned API version and a read-only check (GitHub rate limit,\nJira myself, Vercel user, Ollama tags, Slack URL shape). Status and check\nendpoints drive the Settings page, which now shows what each connector\nenables and whether the saved credential works. Datadog, which nothing\nread, is removed from code, settings, env examples, docs and UI.\n\nA Project is created with every App Studio workspace or imported\nrepository; push records the repo, deploy the deployment, Test this app\nthe requirement, and the build its name, status and spec summary. The\nproject endpoint computes Build, Verify, Review, Release and Operate\nstage statuses from stored runs and deployments. App Studio binds the\ncaller's database on every workspace creation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PYcffsRwcYE3b46A5x4a2o",
        "timestamp": "2026-10-16T16:38:55Z",
